=== PARITY ===
Ported web/src/api/hooks/useChat.ts (2 reads, 3 mutations) -> UI-free KMP state holder
ChatStore over the S7 ChatRepository. Endpoints/params/bodies verified against
web/src/api/devtools.ts (the chat exports useChat wraps), internal/api/router.go
(/chatbot Route block), and internal/api/chatbot/dtos.go (RenameSession 200 {id,title};
DeleteSession 204). Wire types ported verbatim from web/src/api/types.ts.

Reads (2) — cache-then-network StateFlow<Resource<T>>:
 1. useChatSessions -> store.chatSessions()           GET /chatbot/sessions
        -> List<ChatSessionInfo>, cached under CHAT_SESSIONS_KEY ('sessions')
        = web chatKeys.sessions() ['chat','sessions']
 2. useChatHistory  -> store.chatHistory(sessionId)    GET /chatbot/history?session_id={id}
        -> List<ChatMessage>, cached under chatHistoryKey ('history:{id}')
        = web chatKeys.history(id) ['chat','history',id]
        enabled: !!sessionId -> a blank id returns the disabled feed that never fetches
        (asserted: no upstream collection).

Mutations (3):
 3. useRenameChatSession -> store.renameChatSession(sessionId,title)  PATCH /chatbot/sessions/{id}
        body: {title}; id percent-encoded (encodeURIComponent analogue via encodeURLPathPart)
        -> repo optimistic setQueryData patch of the cached session list
           (matching row title = normalizeChatTitle(title)) + store refreshSessions()
 4. useDeleteChatSession -> store.deleteChatSession(sessionId)        DELETE /chatbot/sessions/{id}
        204 No Content -> repo optimistic setQueryData patch (row removed) +
           evict(history key) (removeQueries(history) analogue) + store refreshSessions()
 5. useSendChatMessage  -> store.sendChatMessage(input)               POST /chatbot
        body: {message} (+ session_id only when present; an absent id is dropped from the
        wire body, mirroring JSON.stringify of an undefined value) -> ChatResponse,
        NO cache interaction (web leaves onSuccess to the caller for the typewriter reveal;
        asserted: a send does not refresh the sessions feed).

Optimistic-update/invalidate semantics: web rename/delete call setQueryData (instant local
patch of chatKeys.sessions()) THEN invalidateQueries(chatKeys.sessions()) (refetch). Ported
faithfully: the repository performs the cache patch on the data layer (the setQueryData
analogue) and the store's refreshSessions() bumps the sessions feed's trigger (the
invalidate analogue) — so the refresh's Loading emission carries the already-corrected list
while the network reload runs, and cacheThenNetwork always re-fetches so no stale value is
served as fresh. A failed mutation leaves the cache untouched (asserted). A feed nobody
observes is a no-op refresh (asserted).

Derivations golden-locked (KMP+C# parity, ChatGoldenTest, ADR-004):
  - normalizeChatTitle    (trim; empty/all-whitespace -> null; inner spaces kept)
  - applyRenameToSessions (matching row's title normalised, others untouched, no-match unchanged)
  - applyDeleteToSessions (matching row removed, no-match unchanged)
  - chatHistoryKey / chatHistoryQuery (web chatKeys.history tuple + session_id snake_case query)

SI preserved: chat fields are ids/timestamps/titles/message text — not unit-bearing — so they
round-trip verbatim (sessions cached as typed List<ChatSessionInfo>, history as
List<ChatMessage>, each decoded per-feed off a raw JsonElement partition); conversion is
display-only (S5). New cache domain Chat = 30s (web useChat uses default staleTime 0 = always
refetch on mount and never polls; 30s keeps the freshness flag honest without thrashing while
cacheThenNetwork still refetches on every refresh).

